From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Renaud Deraison <rderaison@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 06:11:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] vhost-user-fs: snapshot and restore

A VM with vhost-user-fs shares can be snapshotted, and restored onto a
fresh backend at the same socket:

- Before the state is saved (vCPUs paused), each fs device stops its rings
  (GET_VRING_BASE) and takes its backend's state through
  VHOST_USER_PROTOCOL_F_DEVICE_STATE (SET_DEVICE_STATE_FD save +
  CHECK_DEVICE_STATE), now negotiated. A backend without it refuses the
  snapshot.
- The saved device: its virtio state, each ring's base, the backend's
  state blob. On restore it connects to the backend, gets its rings set up
  at the saved bases (not the guest's avail index), the state loaded while
  the rings are stopped, then kicked.
- With fs devices the snapshot's memory file is mapped shared: the backend
  maps guest memory through the same file, and must see the guest's writes
  (resume such a snapshot once).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
